{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your care team doctors. I understand you've been having some trouble eating since your last discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Doctor. Every time I try to eat, my stomach starts to ache, especially around the belly button area. I just don’t feel like eating at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned it started about 10 days ago, after your last hospital stay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. I was doing okay at first, but then the pain came back, and I’ve lost my appetite. I also noticed looser stools lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you. You’re not having nausea, vomiting, fevers, or jaundice, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. Just the stomach ache and not feeling hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history with the liver transplant and the biliary stent, we want to make sure nothing’s blocking or irritating your digestive tract."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. But I’m worried—could this be another stricture?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked with a CT scan today, and the biliary stents are still in place and unchanged. No signs of new blockage or free air, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s good to hear. What about that fluid they mentioned near my duodenum?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT did show a small area of fluid near the duodenal bulb, but it looks like it’s inside the bowel, not a collection pressing on it. It’s likely not the main cause of your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think you're not getting enough nutrition because of the pain when you eat. The team is concerned about 'failure to thrive.' We’d like to place a feeding tube to help you get proper nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A feeding tube? Through the nose again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a Dobhoff tube. We’ll place it past your stomach, into the small intestine—post-pyloric—so it bypasses the area that might be sensitive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll numb your nose and throat. You might feel some pressure, but it shouldn’t be painful. It’s done under X-ray guidance to make sure it’s placed correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-07-03 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I trust you. Let’s do it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The tube was placed successfully yesterday under fluoroscopy. It’s now in the correct position in your duodenum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, already? I didn’t feel much. Is it working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we started tube feeds this morning. You’re getting Isosource 1.5 cal at 55 ml per hour. Nutrition says you’re tolerating it well—no nausea or bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But I still have that right-sided pain—hip, groin, sometimes flank. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we reviewed that. The CT showed a small right inguinal hernia, but your pain isn’t always there. Urology checked and said it’s not related to your penile implant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Chronic pain service thinks it’s neuropathic or musculoskeletal. They recommended a Lidoderm patch for the right hip area and increasing gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been on gabapentin before. Isn’t that hard on the liver?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. We actually decided to stop gabapentin to avoid too many medications. Instead, we’re starting nortriptyline at night—it helps with both nerve pain and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having trouble sleeping too. Maybe that will help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Geriatrics also recommended increasing your mirtazapine from 7.5 to 15 mg at bedtime. It can help with both appetite and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. But I’m still worried about my stomach. Why does it hurt when I eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-07-04 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be related to your history of esophageal dysmotility and hiatal hernia. The tube feeds bypass the stomach, so we can give your GI tract a rest while you get nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-07-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. Creatinine is 1.4, down from 1.6—your kidneys are doing better. Liver enzymes are slightly up but not concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-07-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any word on the infection test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-07-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture showed mixed bacteria, but it’s likely contamination from skin or genital area. No sign of real infection, so no antibiotics needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-07-05 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Phew. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. The pain is improving, especially with the nortriptyline. You’re walking more, and the Lidoderm patch seems to help the hip pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s not gone, but it’s better when I move around. I even tried a little food yesterday—no pain, but I didn’t eat much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We want you to keep using the tube feed for at least 20 hours a day for now. We’ll recheck in clinic and maybe adjust later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds? I noticed a change in my CellCept."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we switched from mycophenolate mofetil (CellCept) to Myfortic. It’s the same family but easier on the stomach. We made sure your pharmacy has it before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-07-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I had a lot of stomach issues with the old one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day—we’re getting ready to discharge you. You’re alert, walking independently, pain is manageable, and you’re tolerating the tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. But I want to make sure I do this right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Keep the tube feeding going—20 hours a day. Flush the tube with 30 cc of water if it stops or before and after meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the transplant office if you have fever over 101, vomiting, severe pain, or issues with the incision. No driving while on tramadol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the Lidoderm patch?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One patch daily on the painful area—on for 12 hours, off for 12. And keep taking the new mirtazapine and nortriptyline at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-07-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. We’ll see you in follow-up. Keep building your strength and keep in touch."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-07-03 16:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-07-07 20:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient, status post liver transplant with a history of biliary stricture treated with stent placement, was readmitted 10 days after discharge for failure to thrive and postprandial abdominal pain. He reported decreased oral intake, early satiety, and intermittent supraumbilical discomfort. Imaging confirmed stable biliary stents and no acute abdominal process, though a small fluid area near the duodenum was noted. A post-pyloric Dobhoff tube was placed under fluoroscopic guidance, and enteral feeding was initiated successfully. Chronic right-sided pain, possibly neuropathic, improved with nortriptyline and a Lidoderm patch, while gabapentin was discontinued to reduce polypharmacy. Depression and insomnia were addressed with an increased dose of mirtazapine. Myfortic replaced mycophenolate mofetil due to gastrointestinal side effects. The patient stabilized, tolerated tube feeds, and was discharged home with instructions for ongoing nutrition, medication management, and follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Adult failure to thrive",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Diaphragmatic hernia without mention of obstruction or gangrene",
      "Cryptogenic end stage liver disease",
      "Liver replaced by transplant"
    ]
  }
}
